Z||000000||slick||06-01-99||06:53 PM||||hello, i have read the hot start discussion and am going to try some of the suggestions<br>to alleviate my 88 2.5l's hot start difficulties.Now for my stupid question-<br>where is the tach filter on an 88 2.5l?<br>the tach sometimes bounces around or quits working. could this and the hot start problems be related? thanks!
Z||000001||theogre||06-02-99||07:30 AM||||87+ 2.5 use distributor less DIS ignition, and the I can tell, there is no seperate tach filter on these.<p>you could have a grounding problem on the block, a flaky controller or coil in the DIS pack, a bad/dirty connector on the DIS unit, or posibly an over hot or other wise flaky ECM.<p>your best starting point is to make sure you have fuel pressure. There is a problem with the fuel pumps on many 87-89 Fiero, 6000, and (i think) Grand Am.<p>If Fuel Pressure and all the DIS & ground connections are good, including plug wires, etc, then the coils are easy to change, but it sounds like maybe the DIS controller.
